# The play checks of PLAYCHECK=sample (csrc/Makefile): these snapshot
# recordings, and every one with a clientview.jsonl or cwhash.txt. Kept by
# hand, above the cover line: each recording a play-only failure was found
# on (DEVLOG 2026-09-28, lane/playcheck). The client-view ones
# (idx-clientview-s1, idx-spawner-s1, idx-lead-s1, idx-blast-s1,
# idx-pickup-s1: lane/idxworld) and the client-light ones (idx-cwlight-s1,
# idx-cwcheck-s1) join through their files. A name followed by +live (or
# +live:T,T... for frames after rows T too) also plays its whole tape the
# live way after the check (tests/play_check.sh).
auditfixa-rain-s1      # lane/playfix: play's own tick copy, row 37 d.ents
combat-mobs-s1         # lane/playfix: play's own tick copy, row 2074 d.ents
cg-combat-pig-s1       # lane/playfix (as combat-pig-s1): play's own tick copy, row 458 d.ents
death-keepinv-s1       # lane/playfix: keepInventory passed as 0, row 128 w.ents
mobattack-overlap-s1   # lane/playfix: play's own tick copy, row 3 d.ents
pf-rain-g14            # lane/playfix's weather and difficulty after the world tick (found on auditfixa-rain-s1, which no longer shows it; planted back it fails here, row 1340 d.ents)
moon-swamp-s2 +live    # lane/playarena: the live replay kept every dead living (no grave), arena full at row 555
swamp-night-s2 +live   # lane/playarena: the same, and the grave's sweep faulting on a thread stack's guard page
tnt-cannon-s1 +live:68 # lane/playarena: a section of 3,739 cauldrons past the mesher's buffer (half of Tessellator.instance's)
